WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.261
Welcome. This is your ten-day plan for two-syllable words: long words with two beats.

2
00:00:05.711 --> 00:00:11.945
A long word is two short pieces put together. Each piece is a beat. Here is one, sound by sound.

3
00:00:17.981 --> 00:00:19.151
The word is rabbit.

4
00:00:20.051 --> 00:00:28.722
The goal of this plan is a child who splits a long word into beats, reads each beat, and puts it back together, with words never seen before.

5
00:00:29.322 --> 00:00:35.010
That is the goal. It is not a promise. Day ten is a check, and it shows you where your child is.

6
00:00:35.810 --> 00:00:40.503
This plan is for a child who reads short words, even words like ship and frog.

7
00:00:40.953 --> 00:00:44.248
Often the child guesses a long word from its first letters.

8
00:00:44.698 --> 00:00:47.901
Or freezes at words like rabbit, napkin and jumping.

9
00:00:48.351 --> 00:00:53.428
It is a normal step. A long word has more letters than the eyes can sound out at once.

10
00:00:53.878 --> 00:00:58.317
So this plan teaches one move. Split it, read each beat, put it back together.

11
00:00:58.767 --> 00:01:03.272
Here is what is inside. Ten days. One page a day, about ten minutes.

12
00:01:03.672 --> 00:01:08.816
Day one is a short check. It shows you where to start. Day ten shows you what changed.

13
00:01:09.266 --> 00:01:14.523
Every day has a short video like this one, for you. It shows you what to do before you do it.

14
00:01:15.123 --> 00:01:22.594
Days two, three and four teach the easiest splits: two small words in one, an ending, and two letters the same in the middle.

15
00:01:23.044 --> 00:01:27.162
Day five is a halfway check. It tells you to go on, or to go back.

16
00:01:27.612 --> 00:01:33.422
Days six, seven and eight: two different letters in the middle, finding the split alone, and bigger beats.

17
00:01:33.872 --> 00:01:37.033
On day nine, long words in sentences, and a story.

18
00:01:37.483 --> 00:01:42.316
Some days will need a second try. Doing a page twice is not falling behind.

19
00:01:42.916 --> 00:01:47.260
When a word goes wrong, do not say the word. Say the same words, every time.

20
00:01:47.710 --> 00:01:52.438
Cover the second beat with a finger. Read the first one. Then uncover the rest.

21
00:01:53.338 --> 00:01:59.825
Here is how each day works. First, watch that day's video. Scan the code on the page with your phone.

22
00:02:00.275 --> 00:02:06.189
Then read the yellow box at the top of the page. It gives you three short steps, with the words to say.

23
00:02:06.639 --> 00:02:09.786
Do the first job together. That takes about two minutes.

24
00:02:10.236 --> 00:02:14.555
Then your child carries on with the page, and reads three things to you at the end.

25
00:02:15.005 --> 00:02:19.781
On four of the days your child has a track to listen to. You press play and step away.

26
00:02:20.581 --> 00:02:25.708
You need the printed pages, a pencil, crayons, and scissors for the cards on day two.

27
00:02:26.158 --> 00:02:31.247
When you are ready, start with day one. It is a short check, and it takes about four minutes.
